# Configure SCIM

Loom exposes SCIM routes under `/api/scim` for IdP provisioning.

## 1. Configure SCIM token and server URL

```bash
export LOOM_SERVER_SCIM_TOKEN="replace-with-strong-random-token"
export LOOM_SERVER_HTTP_BASE_URL="https://loom.example.com"
```

Ensure the server is reachable at the base URL your IdP will call.

## 2. Set IdP SCIM base URL

Use:

```text
https://loom.example.com/api/scim
```

## 3. Validate discovery endpoints

```bash
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $LOOM_SERVER_SCIM_TOKEN" \
  https://loom.example.com/api/scim/ServiceProviderConfig | jq .

curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $LOOM_SERVER_SCIM_TOKEN" \
  https://loom.example.com/api/scim/ResourceTypes | jq .
```

## 4. Validate CRUD operations

Core resources:

- `/api/scim/Users`
- `/api/scim/Users/{id}`
- `/api/scim/Groups`
- `/api/scim/Groups/{id}`
- `/api/scim/Bulk`

Your IdP should be able to create, patch, and delete records using bearer-token auth.

<Callout variant="warning" title="Token handling">
	Treat `LOOM_SERVER_SCIM_TOKEN` as a secret and rotate it on schedule.
</Callout>
